From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kim Hansen <github@kimhansen.dk>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:08:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FileHandle: throwing reads and writes; move can replace an
 existing file

A download onto a full disk raised an Objective-C exception from the legacy
FileHandle.write(_:)/seekToEndOfFile(), which Swift cannot catch, so the
process terminated (RumskrotNavigator#244). Reads and writes now use the
throwing calls. move(from:to:replaceIfExists:) sends FileRenameInformation
with ReplaceIfExists, so a client can swap a finished file over an existing
one instead of deleting it first (RumskrotNavigator#242).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LkMKuG84EaZ3Qi6prSGaER
